Correct gwcli.py's stale __version__ string to match the actual release.

gwcli.py hardcodes __version__ = '2.7', which `gwcli --version` reports
verbatim. setup.py's own version (what the sdist/wheel/tag are actually
named) is '3.9'; __version__ was simply never bumped alongside it -- this
is still true as of upstream's current main branch, i.e. it isn't a value
that's deliberately tracking something else. Correct it to match the
packaged release.

--- a/gwcli.py
+++ b/gwcli.py
@@ -17,7 +17,7 @@
 import ceph_iscsi_config.settings as settings

 __author__ = 'Paul Cuzner'
-__version__ = '2.7'
+__version__ = '3.9'


 class GatewayCLI(ConfigShell):
